{"title":"Hope Is a Risk","link":"https://kottke.org/25/06/hope-is-a-risk","date":1750964072000,"content":"\n        <p>From <a href=\"https://colearthurriley.com/\">Cole Arthur Riley</a>, author of <a href=\"https://bookshop.org/a/2966/9780593593646\">Black Liturgies</a> (<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0593593642/ref=nosim/0sil8\">Amazon</a>):</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/regulate-dreaming.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/regulate-dreaming.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/regulate-dreaming.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1350\" alt=\"Hope is a risk; especially when you've known what it is to dream for better and only be met with the tyranny of degradation, greed, and violent appetites. But despair is a concession. Be careful of who you let regulate your dreaming. Always remember who benefits from our hopelessness.\" /></p>\n\n<blockquote><p>Hope is a risk; especially when you’ve known what it is to dream for better and only be met with the tyranny of degradation, greed, and violent appetites.</p>\n\n<p>But despair is a concession.</p>\n\n<p>Be careful of who you let regulate your dreaming. Always remember who benefits from our hopelessness.</p></blockquote>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Cole%20Arthur%20Riley\">Cole Arthur Riley</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/06/hope-is-a-risk\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"1003a3e137833f2884fe744721caccad32d5bddbcb30e6cbd27def6ca9c7d218","category":"Sites"}